problems.description_md:
`src/lib.rs` holds a generic `Shelf<T>`: `new`, `add` and `len` work for any `T`, and `find(key)` works when `T` implements the trait `Keyed`. `find` returns the **first** item added with that key, or `None`. `Item { id, label }` implements `Keyed` with its `id`. The shelf's `items` field is private.

This time you test from outside, as a user of the library would. Files in a `tests/` folder are **integration tests**: Cargo compiles each one as its own crate, which uses the library by name, `test_lab`, and sees only its public items (Book ch. 11.3, "Integration Tests"). `src/lib.rs` is read-only in this problem; your tests go in `tests/shelf.rs`, which needs no `#[cfg(test)]` and no `mod tests`.

Write tests that check:

- items are found by their own key, wherever they are on the shelf (first, middle, last);
- with two items with the same key, `find` returns the one added first;
- a key that isn't there gives `None`, and the ids at the ends of `u32`, 0 and `u32::MAX`, are ordinary keys;
- `len` counts every `add`, and adding never removes earlier items;
- a `Shelf<String>` works too: storing needs no `Keyed`.

`Item` doesn't implement `Debug` or `PartialEq`, so compare its fields: take the item out of the `Option` with `match` (or `if let`) and check `item.label`.

